{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semantic distance semantic distance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md","fileName":"Semantic Distance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semantic Distance","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Game Interactivity]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interactivity","Feedback","Player Mental Model","Articulatory Distance","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semantic distance semantic distance","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md","fileName":"Semantic Distance.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Semantic Distance","heading":"Semantic Distance","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Semantic distance is the gap between feedback presented by a system and the meaning a player must derive from it. Clear, contextual signals shorten this distance; obscure or indirect signals make the player spend more effort interpreting state.\n\nReducing semantic distance helps [[Feedback]] update the [[Player Mental Model]] quickly. Together with low [[Articulatory Distance]], it keeps the interactive loop focused on the game rather than on operating the interface.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Game Interactivity","Feedback","Player Mental Model","Articulatory Distance","advancedgamedesign.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Semantic Distance.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"semantic distance sem